                "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued October 13 at 1:51AM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK",
                "description": "Thursday into the weekend, a series of low pressure systems will\nmove toward Southeast Alaska, bringing widespread moderate to heavy\nrainfall and gale force winds to the Gulf. Strong winds are also\nexpected for coastal and southern panhandle communities. While the\nexact timing and impacts of the system are still being refined,\nconfidence is continuing to increase that this will be a more\nimpactful system for Southeast Alaska.\n\nStay tuned to weather.gov/juneau as we continue to monitor the\ndeveloping situation and update our forecast.",
